{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Java and Python SDKs will be developed as standalone libraries mirroring the capabilities of the existing NodeJS SDK.",
    "Pre-built chaincode deployment (U3) will be implemented using external chaincode deployment via Docker containers, allowing peers to run pre-built images without source code.",
    "VSCC logging enhancements (U4) will be implemented at the INFO level and will include structured logging for policy details, satisfied signers, and lacking signers.",
    "Binary distribution (U5) will leverage CI/CD pipelines to cross-compile Go binaries and publish them to GitHub Releases for various OS/architectures.",
    "Certificate fingerprint validation (U6) will use the 'Load certificate fingerprint list into the channel' approach to avoid non-determinism during endorsement and commit.",
    "Configuration consolidation (U8) will involve creating a 'config_defaults' directory and programmatically extracting or manually migrating all default values from source code into the respective YAML files."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer is highly experienced with Hyperledger Fabric, Go, Java, and Python.",
    "The mention of 'NodeJS' in U1 and U2 is a typo in the specification and implies developing SDKs similar to the existing NodeJS SDK.",
    "Existing CI/CD infrastructure is available and can be modified for binary distribution.",
    "Unit and integration testing efforts are included within the respective activity estimates.",
    "No UI development is required; all work is backend, SDK, CLI, tooling, or configuration-related."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Java SDK Development",
      "activity_description": "Develop a Java SDK to interact with the Hyperledger Fabric blockchain, mirroring NodeJS SDK capabilities including connection, transaction submission, and event listening.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Python SDK Development",
      "activity_description": "Develop a Python SDK to interact with the Hyperledger Fabric blockchain, mirroring NodeJS SDK capabilities including connection, transaction submission, and event listening.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Pre-built Chaincode Deployment",
      "activity_description": "Implement the ability to deploy user chaincode in pre-built form (Docker images) so peers do not need to build the UCC or have the source code. Includes modifying peer logic and build scripts.",
      "most_likely_effort": 60
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "VSCC Logging Enhancements",
      "activity_description": "Improve VSCC validation failure logging to display the policy being used, names of signers/orgs, and lacking signers at the INFO level. Also provide this information to the SDK or event failure notification processes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Platform-Specific Binary Distribution",
      "activity_description": "Setup CI/CD pipelines to build and provide downloadable platform-specific binaries for all tools (configtxgen, fabric-chaintool, fabric-ca client, etc.).",
      "most_likely_effort": 30
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Certificate Fingerprint Validation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the ability for a channel to independently confirm the validity of certificates issued by a Fabric CA by loading a signed certificate fingerprint list into the channel configuration and validating against it.",
      "most_likely_effort": 50
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Network Spin-up Tooling & Docs",
      "activity_description": "Create tools and readme files in the fabric/test/ directory to allow testers to quickly spin up a network, and update the official documentation with links and instructions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 25
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Configuration Consolidation",
      "activity_description": "Consolidate all default configurations into a 'config_defaults' directory. Ensure core.yaml, orderer.yaml, and configtx.yaml contain ALL default values, removing the need to refer to source code.",
      "most_likely_effort": 35
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 400
  }
}
```

